# Trivy findings accepted after review. Each entry needs a reason, and is removed as soon
# as a fix reaches the version line we run (Spring Boot 3.5 / Spring Framework 6.2).

# CVE-2026-47884 (spring-webmvc, CRITICAL): remote code execution through XsltView path
# handling. Fixed only in Spring Framework 7.0.9, a major upgrade. No service uses XsltView
# or any XSLT view, so the vulnerable code path is never reached. Reviewed 2026-10-08.
CVE-2026-47884

# CVE-2026-47890 (spring-webmvc, scored CRITICAL by NVD, LOW by Spring): corrupted Server-Sent
# Event streams when view fragments are rendered over SSE. Fixed only in Spring Framework 7.0.9,
# a major upgrade. Our only SSE is the coach stream (SseEmitter sending JSON); no service renders
# views or fragments (no template engine, no FragmentsRendering), so the code path is never
# reached. https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-47890 Reviewed 2026-10-09.
CVE-2026-47890
